.\" Manpage for herdr-new
.TH HERDR-NEW 1 "October 6, 2026" "202610061700-git" "herdr-new"

.SH NAME
herdr-new \- Create and attach named herdr sessions from environment presets

.SH SYNOPSIS
herdr-new [options] [preset|command] [tab:command ...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a herdr session with one workspace and one tab per window of a preset, runs each tab's command in its pane, and attaches the terminal. A running session with the same name is reused. A stopped session is restarted, and herdr restores its layout.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B <preset> [tab:command ...]
Create (or attach to) a session from a preset. Extra "tab:command" arguments replace the preset's tabs.
.TP
.B list
List sessions.
.TP
.B show
List sessions (same output as list).
.TP
.B attach <session>
Attach to a running or stopped session.
.TP
.B status
Show the herdr server status.
.TP
.B kill <session>
Stop and delete a session.
.TP
.B kill all
Stop every running session.
.TP
.B kill workspace|tab|pane <session> <id>
Close one workspace, tab or pane inside a session.
.TP
.B config check|create|edit|reload|reset-keys
Validate, create, edit, reload or reset the herdr config.toml.
.TP
.B \-\-exec git|uptime|weather|keybindings
Run a helper command, for use in a pane or from the shell.

.SH PRESETS
.TP
.B single, shell, ai
One tab.
.TP
.B dev
Tabs: dev, editor, logging, server.
.TP
.B go
Tabs: main (go run .), test (go test ./...), mod (go mod tidy), editor, docs (go doc).
.TP
.B rust
Tabs: build, run, test, editor, clippy, fmt.
.TP
.B python
Tabs: main, test, venv, editor, jupyter.
.TP
.B node, bun, deno
Tabs: devel, editor, server, database.
.TP
.B devops
Tabs: kubectl, docker, terraform, ansible.
.TP
.B monitoring
Tabs: htop, logs, docker, network, disk.
.TP
.B database
Tabs: mysql, postgres, redis, mongo, editor.
.TP
.B build, test, default
Plain shell tabs.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-name <name>
Override the auto-derived session name (preset-directory).
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help message.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display current version.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debugging output.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Remove all formatting from output.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HERDR_NEW_CONFIG_DIR
Directory holding herdr config.toml (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/herdr or ~/.config/herdr).
.TP
.B HERDR_NEW_LOG_DIR
Directory for per-session server logs (default: ~/.local/log/herdr-new).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I
~/.config/herdr/config.toml
herdr configuration, managed by herdr itself.

.SH REQUIRES
herdr and jq.

